WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.533
Privacy preserving AI.

2
00:00:02.833 --> 00:00:08.433
Every enterprise with sensitive data asks these questions, and few engineers can answer them.

3
00:00:09.633 --> 00:00:12.933
Start with the practical answer: confidential computing.

4
00:00:13.233 --> 00:00:14.767
Data goes in encrypted.

5
00:00:15.067 --> 00:00:22.300
It enters a hardware enclave, like Intel TDX, AMD SEV, or NVIDIA confidential GPUs.

6
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.133
Inference runs inside.

7
00:00:24.433 --> 00:00:27.119
Even the cloud operator cannot read the data.

8
00:00:27.119 --> 00:00:28.133
This ships today.

9
00:00:29.333 --> 00:00:32.133
Differential privacy adds calibrated noise.

10
00:00:32.433 --> 00:00:35.433
Compare the output with and without one person's record.

11
00:00:35.733 --> 00:00:39.054
The budget, epsilon, bounds how different they can be.

12
00:00:39.054 --> 00:00:40.100
Smaller is safer.

13
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:42.533
Here is the full map.

14
00:00:42.833 --> 00:00:46.500
Confidential computing and differential privacy are ready now.

15
00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:54.767
Federated learning trains across devices or hospitals without centralizing data, and pairs naturally with differential privacy.

16
00:00:55.067 --> 00:01:01.033
Homomorphic encryption computes on encrypted data, but is a thousand to a million times slower.

17
00:01:02.233 --> 00:01:04.433
Federated learning deserves a picture.

18
00:01:04.733 --> 00:01:06.800
Each hospital trains on its own data.

19
00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.867
Another hospital does the same.

20
00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:12.588
Only model updates are combined into a shared model.

21
00:01:12.588 --> 00:01:14.233
The raw data never moves.

22
00:01:15.433 --> 00:01:19.911
That slowdown is why it only suits small, targeted operations today.

23
00:01:19.911 --> 00:01:23.467
Beautiful mathematics, but not yet practical at scale.

24
00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:29.733
One last item: machine unlearning, removing a person's data from a trained model.

25
00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:36.867
GDPR style rights demand it, but for large models retraining is still the only reliable answer.

26
00:01:38.067 --> 00:01:38.850
Let's recap.

27
00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:41.133
Confidential computing ships today.

28
00:01:41.433 --> 00:01:44.600
Differential privacy bounds any one record's effect.

29
00:01:44.900 --> 00:01:47.100
Federated learning keeps data local.

30
00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:51.036
Homomorphic encryption and unlearning are ones to watch.

31
00:01:51.036 --> 00:01:53.633
Next up: interpretability and alignment.
